---
import { site } from '../site';
import Ink from './Ink.astro';
import Note from './Note.astro';

const l = site.links;
const links = [
  { href: l.cv, label: 'CV (PDF)' },
  l.scholar && { href: l.scholar, label: 'Google Scholar' },
  l.orcid && { href: l.orcid, label: 'ORCID' },
  { href: l.github, label: 'GitHub' },
  { href: l.linkedin, label: 'LinkedIn' },
  { href: `mailto:${site.email}`, label: site.email },
].filter(Boolean) as { href: string; label: string }[];
---

<header class="hero wrap">
  <div class="text">
    <p class="name">Amogh D. Prasanna</p>
    <h1>Teaching noisy quantum hardware to compute <em>correctly.</em></h1>
    <p class="sub">
      {site.role} at the <strong>{site.affiliation}</strong>, working with Prof. Shabnam Jabeen and, at Fermilab's SQMS Center, Dr. Tanay Roy.
    </p>
    <ul class="links mono" aria-label="Links">
      {links.map((x) => <li><a href={x.href}>{x.label}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="side">
    <figure class="spacetime" data-spacetime>
      <canvas tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="Space-time view of a surface code's syndrome history. Drag, or use the arrow keys, to turn it." aria-describedby="spacetime-cap"></canvas>
      <figcaption id="spacetime-cap" class="visually-hidden">
        An example error history on a distance-5 surface code, Z-type checks only, measured over four rounds and stacked with time going up.
        It starts as a single round seen from above, then tilts to show every round at once. Five detection events appear:
        a pair in round 1 from a two-qubit error chain, a pair at the same check in rounds 2 and 3 from one faulty measurement,
        and a single event in round 3 from an error on the edge of the code. A minimum-weight matching pairs the first two sets
        and connects the last to the boundary. Illustrative, not data.
      </figcaption>
      <div class="phases mono">
        <button type="button" data-stage>01 one round</button><button type="button" data-stage>02 all rounds</button><button type="button" data-stage>03 matched</button>
        <button class="replay" type="button" data-replay aria-label="Replay the space-time animation">replay</button>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <div class="working">
      <Ink name="eq-qudit" class="eq" label="Handwritten: U is approximately U N through U 2 U 1, a product of native gates, with U in SU of d." />
      <Note class="n-eq" arrow="left" speak>what I'm working on: a qudit unitary, compiled into native gates</Note>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<script>
  import { mountSpacetime } from '../scripts/spacetime';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-spacetime]').forEach(mountSpacetime);
</script>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-l); align-items: center;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 6.5rem) var(--space-xl);
  }
  .name { font-size: var(--step-1); font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 1.1rem; }
  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-4); line-height: 1.03; font-weight: 340; letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 360; }
  .sub { max-width: 54ch; color: var(--mute); margin-top: 1.6rem; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .sub strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.55rem 1.3rem; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 1.9rem; }
  .links a { color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--faint); padding-bottom: 2px; }
  .links a:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .links li:last-child a { text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0.02em; }

  .side { position: relative; }
  .spacetime { position: relative; margin: 0; }
  canvas { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 13 / 10; cursor: grab; touch-action: pan-y; }
  canvas:active { cursor: grabbing; }
  .phases { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0 1.2rem; align-items: center; padding-left: 9%; margin-top: -0.2rem; }
  .phases button { white-space: nowrap; }
  .phases [data-stage] {
    background: none; border: 0; padding: 0.4rem 0; cursor: pointer; color: var(--mute);
    font: inherit; letter-spacing: inherit; text-transform: inherit; transition: color 0.3s;
  }
  .phases [data-stage]:hover, .phases :global(.on) { color: var(--fg); }
  .replay {
    margin-left: auto; background: none; border: 0; color: var(--mute); cursor: pointer;
    font: inherit; letter-spacing: inherit; text-transform: inherit; padding: 0.4rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--faint);
  }
  .replay:hover { color: var(--fg); }

  .working { margin-top: var(--space-m); display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; justify-items: start; }
  .working :global(.eq) { width: min(100%, 29rem); }
  .working :global(.n-eq) { font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 1.15rem + 0.5vw, 1.6rem); max-width: 100%; transform: rotate(-1.5deg); margin-left: 0.5rem; }

  /* On a phone: name and statement first, then the array, then the details. */
  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0; padding-top: 1.75rem; }
    .text { display: contents; }
    .name { order: 1; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
    h1 { order: 2; }
    .side { order: 3; max-width: 30rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
    .phases { padding-left: 0; gap: 0 0.9rem; }
    .sub { order: 4; }
    .links { order: 5; }
  }
</style>
